        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Myxomatous mitral valve is defined as the presence of excess leaflet tissue and leaflet thickening greater than 5 mm, resulting in a prolapse greater than 2 mm into the left atrium on parasternal long axis view.</babelon:source_value>
