        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Retinitis pigmentosa inversa is form of retinal degeneration characterized by areas of retinal/chorioretinal degeneration with pigment migration in the macular area (in contrast to retinitis pigmentosa which, at early disease stages, predominantly affects the retinal periphery)</babelon:source_value>
