    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0008352">
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="tr">Trombositlerin bağlanmasında anormallik. Normalde, trombositler, glikoproteinlerle ve GPVI&apos;den oluşan bir reseptör vasıtasıyla veya vWF&apos;ye reseptör GPIb/IX/V aracılığıyla hasarlanmadan saniye içinde vasküler subendotelyumdaki kollajene bağlanırlar. daha sonra da bağlanma eğilimindeki trombositler trombosit aktivasyonuna ve toplanmasına yol açan granülleri serbest bırakır</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="tr">Bozulmuş trombosit adezyonu</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0008352"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="tr">Trombositlerin bağlanmasında anormallik. Normalde, trombositler, glikoproteinlerle ve GPVI&apos;den oluşan bir reseptör vasıtasıyla veya vWF&apos;ye reseptör GPIb/IX/V aracılığıyla hasarlanmadan saniye içinde vasküler subendotelyumdaki kollajene bağlanırlar. daha sonra da bağlanma eğilimindeki trombositler trombosit aktivasyonuna ve toplanmasına yol açan granülleri serbest bırakır</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>An abnormality of adhesion of thrombocytes. Normally, platelets adhere to collagen in the vascular subendothelium within seconds of injury via a receptor made up of glycoprotein Ia and IIa and GPVI and to vWF via receptor GPIb/IX/V. The adherent platelets then release granules that lead to platelet activation and aggregation.</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>CANDIDATE</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0008352"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="tr">Bozulmuş trombosit adezyonu</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Impaired platelet adhesion</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>OFFICIAL</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0008353">
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="tr">İdrarda anormal olarak artmış nötral amino asit konsantrasyonu varlığı. Nötral aminoasitler triptofan, alanin, asparajin, glutamin, histidin, izolösin, lösin, fenilalanin, serin, treonin, tirozin ve valindir</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="tr">Nötral hiperaminoasidüri</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0008353"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="tr">İdrarda anormal olarak artmış nötral amino asit konsantrasyonu varlığı. Nötral aminoasitler triptofan, alanin, asparajin, glutamin, histidin, izolösin, lösin, fenilalanin, serin, treonin, tirozin ve valindir</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>The presence of an abnormally increased concentration of neutral amino acids in the urine. The neutral amino acids are tryptophan, alanine, asparagine, glutamine, histidine, isoleucine, leucine, phenylalanine, serine, threonine, tyrosine and valine.</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>OFFICIAL</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0008353"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="tr">Nötral hiperaminoasidüri</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Neutral hyperaminoaciduria</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>OFFICIAL</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0008354">
