        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Linear nevus sebaceous</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>OFFICIAL</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010818">
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="tr">Bir kaç saniyeden dakikalar içinde sonlanan kas kasılmasında uzamış artış ile olan genel nöbetler</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="tr">Genel tonik nöbetler</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010818"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="tr">Bir kaç saniyeden dakikalar içinde sonlanan kas kasılmasında uzamış artış ile olan genel nöbetler</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>A generalized tonic seizure is a type of generalized motor seizure characterized by bilateral limb stiffening or elevation, often with neck stiffening without a subsequent clonic phase. The tonic activity can be a sustained abnormal posture, either in extension or flexion, sometimes accompanied by tremor of the extremities.</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>CANDIDATE</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010818"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="tr">Genel tonik nöbetler</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Generalized tonic seizure</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>CANDIDATE</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010819">
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="tr">Kas tonusunun ani kaybı veya azalması ile karakterize, parçalı bir segmente (ekstremiteler, çene, kafa) sınırlı veya masif, yere düşmeye yol açan nöbetler</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="tr">Atonik nöbetler</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010819"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="tr">Kas tonusunun ani kaybı veya azalması ile karakterize, parçalı bir segmente (ekstremiteler, çene, kafa) sınırlı veya masif, yere düşmeye yol açan nöbetler</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Atonic seizure is a type of motor seizure characterized by a sudden loss or diminution of muscle tone without apparent preceding myoclonic or tonic event lasting about 1 to 2 seconds, involving head, trunk, jaw, or limb musculature.</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>CANDIDATE</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010819"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="tr">Atonik nöbetler</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Atonic seizure</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>CANDIDATE</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010820">
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="tr">Ana özellik olarak ağlama veya ağlama feveranı ile karaktarize bir nöbet tipi</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="tr">Dakrisistik nöbetler</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010820"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="tr">Ana özellik olarak ağlama veya ağlama feveranı ile karaktarize bir nöbet tipi</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Focal emotional seizure with crying (dacrystic) is characterized by the presence of stereotyped crying, this may be accompanied by lacrimation, sad facial expression and sobbing. The subjective emotion of sadness may or may not be present.</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>CANDIDATE</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010820"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="tr">Dakrisistik nöbetler</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Focal emotional seizure with crying</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>CANDIDATE</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010821">
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="tr">Ana özellik olarak gülme veya gülme feveranı ile karaktarize bir nöbet tipi</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="tr">Kahkaha nöbetleri</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010821"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="tr">Ana özellik olarak gülme veya gülme feveranı ile karaktarize bir nöbet tipi</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Focal emotional seizure with laughing (gelastic) is characterized by bursts of laughter or giggling, usually without appropriate related emotion of happiness, and described as &apos;mirthless&apos;.</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>CANDIDATE</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010821"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="tr">Kahkaha nöbetleri</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Focal emotional seizure with laughing</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>CANDIDATE</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010822">
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="tr">Parıldayan bir skotom, görüş alanların merkezine yakın bir yerde titreşen ışık vasıtasıyla migren öncesinde görülebilen yaygın bir görsel auradır. Nokta, görüşü engeller ve bu yüzden skotom olarak adlandırılır. Skotom, beyaz veya renkli yanıp sönen ışıkların bir yada birden fazla parlayan arkına uzanabilir</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="tr">Işıldayan skotom</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010822"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="tr">Parıldayan bir skotom, görüş alanların merkezine yakın bir yerde titreşen ışık vasıtasıyla migren öncesinde görülebilen yaygın bir görsel auradır. Nokta, görüşü engeller ve bu yüzden skotom olarak adlandırılır. Skotom, beyaz veya renkli yanıp sönen ışıkların bir yada birden fazla parlayan arkına uzanabilir</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>A scintillating scotoma is a common visual aura that can precede a migraine, whereby a spot of flickering light near the center of the visual fields occurs. The spot prevents vision, and is thus termed scotoma. The scotoma can extend into one or more shimmering arcs of white or colored flashing lights.</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>CANDIDATE</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010822"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="tr">Işıldayan skotom</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Scintillating scotoma</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>OFFICIAL</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010823">
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="tr">Bir sütçocuğunda erken kapanma ile birlikte veya olmaksızın kafatası kemik plakaların üst üste gelmesi</obo:IAO_0000115>
