        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>CANDIDATE</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010877">
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="tr">Sadece bir gözün etkilendiği bir strabismus tipi. Unilateral strabismus değişik zamanlarda hiç bir gözün şaşı bakmadığı değişken strabismustan ayrılmalıdır</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="tr">Monoküler strabismus</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010877"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="tr">Sadece bir gözün etkilendiği bir strabismus tipi. Unilateral strabismus değişik zamanlarda hiç bir gözün şaşı bakmadığı değişken strabismustan ayrılmalıdır</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>A type of strabismus in which the fixating eye is always the same one, while the other eye is constantly deviated. Monocular strabismus is to be distinguished from alternating strabismus, in which either of the eyes &apos;squints&apos; at different times.</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>OFFICIAL</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010877"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="tr">Monoküler strabismus</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Monocular strabismus</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>OFFICIAL</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010878">
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="tr">Birden fazla septum ile kistik bir kütlenin prenatal dönem boyunca varlığı, çoklu asimetrik ile, boyunun posterior görünümü yakınında ince duvarlı kistler. Fetal kistik higroma, 3.0 mm&apos;den büyük septasyonlar olan veya olmayan nükal yarı saydamlık olarak tanımlanabilir</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="tr">Fetal kistik higroma</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010878"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="tr">Birden fazla septum ile kistik bir kütlenin prenatal dönem boyunca varlığı, çoklu asimetrik ile, boyunun posterior görünümü yakınında ince duvarlı kistler. Fetal kistik higroma, 3.0 mm&apos;den büyük septasyonlar olan veya olmayan nükal yarı saydamlık olarak tanımlanabilir</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>The presence during the prenatal period of a cystic mass with multiple septa with multiple, asymmetric, thin-walled cysts near the posterior aspect of the neck. Fetal cystic hygroma can be defined as nuchal translucency with or without septations measuring greater than 3.0 mm. Increased NT refers to a measurement above the 95th centile, and the term is used irrespective of whether the collection of fluid is septated or not, and whether it is confined to the neck or envelopes the whole fetus. After 14 weeks, increased NT usually resolves, but in some cases it evolves into nuchal edema or cystic hygromas.</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>CANDIDATE</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010878"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="tr">Fetal kistik higroma</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Fetal cystic hygroma</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>OFFICIAL</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010879">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="tr">Postnatal kistik higroma</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010879"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="tr">Postnatal kistik higroma</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Postnatal cystic hygroma</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>OFFICIAL</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010880">
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="tr">Posterior fetal boyunda anormal olarak geniş bir hipoekoik boşluk varlığı (sıklıkla prenatal ultrason muayenesinde tespit edilir)</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="tr">Artmış nukhal şeffaflık</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010880"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="tr">Posterior fetal boyunda anormal olarak geniş bir hipoekoik boşluk varlığı (sıklıkla prenatal ultrason muayenesinde tespit edilir)</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Nuchal translucency is the sonographic appearance of subcutaneous accumulation of liquid in the back of the fetal neck in the first trimester of pregnancy (11-14 gestational weeks of pregnancy).</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>CANDIDATE</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010880"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="tr">Artmış nukhal şeffaflık</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Increased nuchal translucency</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>OFFICIAL</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010881">
