        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="tr">Bir saatten fazla süren basit motor bulgular ile bir vücut tarafına sınırlı klonik aktivite ve oldukça düzenli aralıklar ile tekrar eden kısmi epileptik statüsün bir formu</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Epilepsia partialis continua (also called Kojevnikov&apos;s or Kozhevnikov&apos;s epilepsia) is a type of focal motor status epilepticus characterized by repeated stereotyped simple motor manifestations such as jerks, typically of a limb or the face, recurring every few seconds or minutes for extended periods (days or years).</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>CANDIDATE</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
