        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Ankylosis</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>OFFICIAL</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0031014">
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="tr">Genellikle, aorta kemerinden üç büyük arter ortaya çıkar: brakiyosefalik gövde (sağ genel karotid artere ve sağ subklaviyen artere ayrılır), sol genel karotid arteri ve sol subklavian arter. Bununla birlikte, anormal subklavian arter varyantı mevcut olduğunda brakiyosefalik gövde yoktur ve aorta kemerinden dört geniş arter ortaya çıkar: sağ genel karotid arteri, sol genel karotid arteri, sol subklaviyan arter ve son olarak en sol taraf kökenli distal, ayrıca arter lusorya olarak da adlandırılan, subklavian arter</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="tr">Arteria lusoria</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0031014"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="tr">Genellikle, aorta kemerinden üç büyük arter ortaya çıkar: brakiyosefalik gövde (sağ genel karotid artere ve sağ subklaviyen artere ayrılır), sol genel karotid arteri ve sol subklavian arter. Bununla birlikte, anormal subklavian arter varyantı mevcut olduğunda brakiyosefalik gövde yoktur ve aorta kemerinden dört geniş arter ortaya çıkar: sağ genel karotid arteri, sol genel karotid arteri, sol subklaviyan arter ve son olarak en sol taraf kökenli distal, ayrıca arter lusorya olarak da adlandırılan, subklavian arter</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Usually, three large arteries arise from the arch of the aorta: the brachiocephalic trunk (divided into the right common carotid artery and the right subclavian artery), the left common carotid artery, and the left subclavian artery. However, when aberrant right subclavian artery variant is present, the brachiocephalic trunk is absent and four large arteries arise from the arch of the aorta: the right common carotid artery, the left common carotid artery, the left subclavian artery, and the final one with the most distal left sided origin, the right subclavian artery, also called the arteria lusoria</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>CANDIDATE</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0031014"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="tr">Arteria lusoria</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>obsolete Arteria lusoria</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>CANDIDATE</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0031015">
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="tr">Karaciğerin intrahepatik portal venlerinin sklerozu ve genellikle sirotik olmayan portal hipertansiyon ile birlikte bulunur, splenomegali ve varisleri özellik olarak içerebilir</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="tr">İntrahepatik portal ven sklerozu</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0031015"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="tr">Karaciğerin intrahepatik portal venlerinin sklerozu ve genellikle sirotik olmayan portal hipertansiyon ile birlikte bulunur, splenomegali ve varisleri özellik olarak içerebilir</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Sclerosis of the intrahepatic portal veins of the liver and generally accompanied by non-cirrhotic portal hypertension, features of which may include splenomegaly and varices.</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>tr</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>OFFICIAL</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
