        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Juvenile aseptic necrosis comprises a group of orthopedic diseases characterized by interruption of the blood supply of a bone, followed by localized bony necrosis most often of the epiphyses of bones of children or teenagers.</babelon:source_value>
